# CSS & Theming — Zentory IMS

## Design System

All styles live in a single `css/style.css`. The design is built on CSS custom properties defined on `:root`.

Key variables: `--primary`, `--bg`, `--bg-card`, `--text`, `--text-secondary`, `--border`, `--shadow`, `--radius`, `--sidebar-width`, `--topbar-height`.

## Dark Theme

Dark mode overrides are scoped under `[data-theme="dark"]`. When adding a new component:

1. Define its colors using existing CSS variables (`var(--bg-card)`, `var(--text)`, etc.)
2. If the component uses hardcoded colors (badges, icons, charts), add a `[data-theme="dark"] .your-class` override
3. Test both themes — toggled via `document.documentElement.setAttribute('data-theme', 'dark')`

Theme state is stored in `localStorage` key `ims_theme` (`'light'` or `'dark'`).

## Responsive Breakpoints

- **Desktop** (>768px): sidebar visible, bottom nav hidden
- **Mobile** (<=768px): sidebar hidden, `<nav class="bottom-nav">` visible with 5 tabs + "More" sheet

When adding new views, ensure they work at both breakpoints. Use the existing responsive patterns:
- Tables: `overflow-x: auto` wrapper
- Cards: CSS Grid with `repeat(auto-fill, minmax(280px, 1fr))`
- Modals: full-screen on mobile via `max-width:100vw; height:100dvh` at the breakpoint

## Class Naming

Follow the existing flat naming convention (not BEM):
- Layout: `.sidebar`, `.topbar`, `.main-content`, `.bottom-nav`
- Components: `.card`, `.stat-card`, `.data-table`, `.modal`, `.badge`
- Module-specific: prefix with module name — `.pos-item-card`, `.recipe-card`, `.khata-party-card`
- State: `.active`, `.hidden`, `.in-bill`, `.current`
